    {
      "section_id": "regulatory_context",
      "title": "Regulatory and policy context",
      "required": true,
      "body_md": "This section identifies the supervisory guidance that applies to the model and ties each regulatory statement to a knowledge passage. The model is developed and documented under the following supervisory guidance: SR 11-7, SR 26-2 [A:5c2859d2c12245182829390b010502c17d4be5ca8af39e9560b74f695b3bcdd8#regulatory_scope] [K:k_853dddea8b5f] [K:k_b1860ab50e4c]. SR 11-7 established the expectations for model development, implementation, use and validation, including effective challenge and documentation detailed enough for an independent party to understand the model, and this document follows its structure [K:k_853dddea8b5f]. SR 26-2 superseded SR 11-7 and SR 21-8 as the supervisory guidance on model risk management and places generative and agentic AI outside its scope, so the agents that assist in producing this document are governed separately from the model it describes [K:k_b1860ab50e4c].",
