          "passage": {
            "citation_id": "k_853dddea8b5f",
            "doc_id": "modelforge-governance",
            "title": "ModelForge Governance Controls: gates, four-eyes rule, lineage, replay and redaction",
            "section": "ModelForge Governance Controls > Regulatory framing",
            "text": "SR 26-2, issued on April 17, 2026 by the Federal Reserve Board, the OCC and the FDIC, superseded SR 11-7 and SR 21-8. Its text places generative AI and agentic AI models outside its scope, describing them as novel and rapidly evolving, and states that a banking organisation's broader risk management and governance practices should still guide the controls for tools and systems the guidance does not cover. Its principles apply to traditional statistical and quantitative models. Two consequences follow for this system. The PD scorecards it produces are traditional statistical models, so the themes of the guidance (sound development, validation, monitoring, governance and documentation) bear on them. The agentic workflow that helps produce them falls outside that guidance, so the controls below are the system's own application of broader governance practice to an agentic process. They are a design choice, not a claim that the system meets any regulatory standard.",
            "url": "knowledge-base/modelforge-governance.md"
          },
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "marker": "[K:k_b1860ab50e4c]",
