    {
      "section_id": "methodology",
      "title": "Methodology and conceptual soundness",
      "required": true,
      "body_md": "The champion for synthetic_pd [A:5c2859d2c12245182829390b010502c17d4be5ca8af39e9560b74f695b3bcdd8#model_name] is a weight-of-evidence logistic regression scorecard, chosen for its transparency and its monotone, explainable relationship between each feature and the predicted risk. A gradient-boosted model was built on the same features as a challenger to benchmark the discrimination the scorecard gives up for that transparency. Each feature is binned and replaced by the weight of evidence of its bin before estimation. The model estimates the default event over the horizon: five synthetic vintages [A:5c2859d2c12245182829390b010502c17d4be5ca8af39e9560b74f695b3bcdd8#target.horizon].",
