    {
      "section_id": "limitations",
      "title": "Limitations and weaknesses",
      "required": true,
      "body_md": "The default event is a proxy: where the public company-bankruptcy data is used, bankruptcy within the forecast horizon stands in for default, so the model estimates bankruptcy risk rather than credit default as a lender would define it. The modelled horizon is: five synthetic vintages [A:5c2859d2c12245182829390b010502c17d4be5ca8af39e9560b74f695b3bcdd8#target.horizon]. Origination vintages are also a proxy: the dataset's horizon files are treated as vintages, so the out-of-time sample tests stability across forecast horizons rather than across calendar time. These limitations should be read alongside the overall validation outcome of pass [A:86b8f3af768295d1ab7706b31321671c6c4fd86e55a0a59248cd44d48d394f39#overall].",
